	(text "System-5 6845 video card Rev B-Clean-Keyboard, one sheet per functional block:\n  sheet 2  Decode         BUS DECODE: A8-A15 LATCH, 4K BLOCK COMPARE (SV1), RAM AND CRTC SELECTS\n  sheet 3  VRAM+CRTC      DUAL-PORT VIDEO RAM AND THE 6845\n  sheet 4  Clocks         DOT CLOCK AND CHARACTER CLOCK (DIVIDE BY 6)\n  sheet 5  Video          CHARACTER LATCHES, CHARACTER GENERATOR, DOT SHIFTER, PIPELINE, REVERSE VIDEO, COMPOSITE OUT\n  sheet 6  Keyboard bus   THE KEYBOARD ON THE BUS: KEY LATCH (7802), STATUS (7804), KEY-READY, THE FLAG LINE\n  sheet 7  Keyboard       PS/2 KEYBOARD CONTROLLER (VIDEO-G TEXT'S, FIRMWARE embedded/video-g-ps2)\n  sheet 8  Power          POWER, DECOUPLING, LED\n\nRev B-Clean (Rev B, Ken's working card, without the DB9) on the 36-pin bus, with VIDEO-G TEXT's PS/2 keyboard section, 2026-11-20: the 6845 at 7800 / 7801 only, the key at 7802, status at 7804. Redrawn from the board netlist and proven pin for pin against it (gen_schematic.py). IC8 must be a 74LS163.\n\nEvery net of a sheet is a pin of its sheet symbol here, labelled with the net's name. Above a dashed line:\nthe nets the sheet shares with other sheets (left: it reads them, right: it drives them). Below it: nets\ndrawn on that sheet only. VCC and GND are power symbols on the sheets." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 15.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2ee9d255-1af3-5a4b-ae52-abc93bf220ce"))
	(sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
